---
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { t, pathFor, type Lang } from '../i18n';
interface Props { lang: Lang }
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const c = t(lang);
const mail = SITE.contactEmail;
---
<article class="legal wrap narrow">
  {lang === 'zh' ? (
    <Fragment>
      <h1>隐私政策</h1>
      <p class="muted small">{c.legal.updated}：2026-10-15</p>

      <h2>1. 适用范围</h2>
      <p>本政策适用于本网站和千剪 Reelfold 开源软件（桌面应用和 video-studio 技能）。千剪免费、按 MIT 许可开源，由个人开发者 Yun Zi 维护。联系邮箱：<a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>。</p>

      <h2>2. 浏览本网站</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>本站是静态网站，不使用 cookie，不加载广告脚本，不从第三方加载字体，也没有表单。</li>
        <li>我们可能用 Cloudflare Web Analytics 统计浏览量。它不使用 cookie，不保存 IP 地址等个人信息，只给出页面浏览量、来源等合计数。</li>
        <li>托管服务商（Cloudflare）可能按其政策记录访问日志，例如 IP 地址和浏览器信息。我们不会用这些日志识别个人。</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. 桌面应用和开源技能</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>软件在你自己的电脑上运行，剪辑和渲染在本机完成，默认转写也在本地。选择云端转写时，音轨会发送到你配置的转写服务。我们没有服务器接收你的素材。</li>
        <li>为了选段、写标题和校对字幕，逐字稿文本、少量关键帧截图和标题会发给你自己配置的 AI 服务（你的 Claude Code / Codex 订阅、你的 API key，或本地模型）。用 AI 配音或 AI 视频生成（比如可选的 Hedra AI 出镜）时，文本和参考图会发给对应厂商；会花钱的服务，要你确认后才调用。这些数据按你和该服务商之间的条款处理。</li>
        <li>用 Claude Code 或 Codex 订阅时，千剪在你的电脑上运行你自己安装、自己登录的命令行工具，由它按你的订阅条款与 Anthropic 或 OpenAI 通信。应用里的实时窗口只在本机显示它的输出，密钥会被隐去。</li>
        <li>你在请求里贴的链接（网页、公开的 Notion 页面）由你的电脑直接打开读取。导出的 Notion 文件夹和讲稿只在本机读取。</li>
        <li>本地免费配音（英文 Kokoro、下载后的中文 Qwen3-TTS，仅 Apple 芯片）在本机生成，不需要 API Key，也不发送配音文字。</li>
        <li>人脸检测等图像处理（MediaPipe）完全在本机运行，不向任何服务器发送数据。</li>
        <li>检查更新时，应用会访问 GitHub 上的发布页面。</li>
        <li>首次使用时，应用会下载语音识别模型和字体等数据文件（来自 GitHub、Google 存储和 Hugging Face）；初次使用免费配音时，会从 Hugging Face 下载 Kokoro 语音模型（约 330 MB）。下载不附带任何身份信息。</li>
        <li>问题报告：千剪从不自己发送。点“报告这个问题”时，你会先看到完整的报告（路径已缩短，不含文件名、文字稿、提示词或密钥），然后由你在浏览器里打开预填好的 GitHub 页面，自己决定是否发布。</li>
        <li><strong>Mac App Store 版</strong>：没有使用次数统计和自动更新检查。项目文件保存在本机应用容器中；使用配置的云端 AI、云端转写或生成服务时，仍会向对应服务发送上述任务输入。</li>
        <li>匿名使用次数（仅桌面应用，<strong>默认关闭，你主动打开才发送</strong>）：随机 ID、版本号、系统、界面语言、事件名、日期和几个小整数（比如一批跑完了多少条）。不发送文件名、文字或素材，服务器不保存 IP 地址；原始记录 13 个月后删除。在应用的“设置 › 通用 › 隐私”里可以随时关闭，或点“删除我的使用数据”删除已发送的记录。完整字段见<a href="/docs/zh/concepts/usage-counts/">隐私：千剪会发送什么</a>。技能不发送任何使用数据。</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. 联系我们和 GitHub</h2>
      <p>你发给我们的邮件只用于回复你。在 GitHub Discussions 或 Issues 里发的内容是公开的，按 GitHub 的条款处理，请不要贴出私人素材或密钥。</p>

      <h2>5. 你的权利</h2>
      <p>匿名使用数据可以直接在应用里删除（设置 › 通用 › 隐私 › 删除我的使用数据）。你也可以要求查看或删除你发给我们的邮件中的个人信息。发邮件到 <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>，我们会在 7 天内处理并回复确认。</p>

      <h2>6. 变更</h2>
      <p>政策变更时，我们会更新本页日期。</p>
      <p><a href={pathFor(lang)}>{c.legal.back}</a></p>
    </Fragment>
  ) : (
    <div lang={lang !== 'en' ? 'en' : undefined}>
      {lang !== 'en' && <p class="draft-banner" lang={lang} role="note">{c.legal.englishOnly}</p>}
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="muted small">{c.legal.updated}: 2026-10-15</p>

      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>This policy covers this website and the Reelfold open-source software (the desktop app and the video-studio skill). Reelfold is free and open source under the MIT licence, maintained by Yun Zi, an individual developer. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>.</p>

      <h2>2. Visiting this website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>This is a static site. It sets no cookies, loads no ad scripts, loads no third-party fonts and has no forms.</li>
        <li>We may count page views with Cloudflare Web Analytics. It uses no cookies and stores no personal data such as IP addresses; we only see totals such as page views and referrers.</li>
        <li>The hosting provider (Cloudflare) may keep access logs, such as IP address and browser details, under its own policy. We do not use those logs to identify people.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Desktop app and open-source skill</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The software runs on your own computer. Editing, rendering and default transcription run locally. If you select hosted transcription, the audio track goes to the transcription service you configure. We run no server that receives your footage.</li>
        <li>To pick segments, write titles and proofread captions, transcript text, a few keyframe screenshots and titles are sent to the AI service you configure (your Claude Code or Codex subscription, your API keys, or a local model). AI voiceover or AI video generation (such as the optional Hedra presenter) sends text and reference images to that vendor; paid services run only after you approve the spend. That is governed by your terms with the vendor.</li>
        <li>With a Claude Code or Codex subscription, Reelfold runs the command-line tool you installed and signed in to yourself, on your computer; it talks to Anthropic or OpenAI under your plan’s terms. The app’s live pane shows its output on your computer only, with keys hidden.</li>
        <li>Links you paste into a request (web pages, public Notion pages) are fetched directly by your computer. Exported Notion folders and notes are read locally.</li>
        <li>Local free voices (Kokoro for English and downloaded Qwen3-TTS for Chinese, Apple silicon only) run on your computer. They need no API key and send no narration text.</li>
        <li>Face detection and other image processing (MediaPipe) run entirely on your computer and send nothing to any server.</li>
        <li>When it checks for updates, the app contacts the release page on GitHub.</li>
        <li>On first use the app downloads data files such as the speech-recognition model and fonts (from GitHub, Google storage and Hugging Face); the first time you use the free voice, it downloads the Kokoro voice model (about 330 MB) from Hugging Face. No identifiers are sent.</li>
        <li>Problem reports: Reelfold never sends them by itself. “Report this problem” shows you the whole report first (paths shortened; no file names, transcripts, prompts or keys), then opens a prefilled GitHub page in your browser; you decide whether to post it.</li>
        <li><strong>Mac App Store edition</strong>: has no usage counts and no update check. Project files are stored in the app’s container on your Mac. Configured cloud AI, hosted transcription and generation services still receive the task inputs described above when used.</li>
        <li>Anonymous usage counts (desktop app only, <strong>off unless you turn it on</strong>): a random ID, the app version, OS, interface language, the event name, the day and a few small integers (such as how many clips a batch made). No file names, text or footage; the server does not store IP addresses; raw records are deleted after 13 months. Turn it off at any time in Settings › General › Privacy, or press “Delete my usage data” to delete what was sent. Every field is listed in <a href="/docs/concepts/usage-counts/">Privacy: what Reelfold sends</a>. The skill sends no usage data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Contacting us and GitHub</h2>
      <p>Emails you send us are used only to reply to you. Anything you post in GitHub Discussions or Issues is public and handled under GitHub’s terms; please don’t post private footage or keys there.</p>

      <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Anonymous usage data can be deleted from the app itself (Settings › General › Privacy › Delete my usage data). You can also ask to see or delete personal data in emails you sent us. Email <a href={`mailto:${mail}`}>{mail}</a>; we act within 7 days and confirm by reply.</p>

      <h2>6. Changes</h2>
      <p>We update the date on this page when the policy changes.</p>
      <p><a href={pathFor(lang)}>{c.legal.back}</a></p>
    </div>
  )}
</article>
